{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every screen that models its state with "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" already knows exactly when it was opened and when it moves between Empty, Loading, Data, and Error. "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsService","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" turns those moments into "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"s and fans them out to as many "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsTracker","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"s as you register — one per analytics backend (Firebase, Mixpanel, Amplitude, your own logging endpoint, a debug console print, …)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"ScreenStates ships no backend-specific tracker implementations, so the core module stays dependency-free — but it does include ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/PrintScreenAnalyticsTracker"},{"text":" (logs every event to the console) and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/NoOpScreenAnalyticsTracker"},{"text":" (silently discards everything), so you don’t have to hand-roll a console logger just to confirm events fire at the right moments. For a real backend, write one small adapter, converting the event’s backend-agnostic ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/AnalyticsValue"},{"text":" parameters into that SDK’s own format:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct FirebaseScreenTracker: ScreenAnalyticsTracker {","    func track(_ event: ScreenAnalyticsEvent) {","        Analytics.logEvent(event.name, parameters: event.parameters.mapValues { value in","            switch value {","            case .string(let string): string","            case .int(let int): int","            case .double(let double): double","            case .bool(let bool): bool","            }","        })","    }","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An adapter is also free to remap ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event.name"},{"text":" to whatever vocabulary its backend expects — Firebase, for example, reserves a specific constant for screen views.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Wiring a screen","level":2,"anchor":"Wiring-a-screen"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let analytics = ScreenAnalyticsService(trackers: [FirebaseScreenTracker(), PrintScreenAnalyticsTracker()])","","func onAppear(source: ScreenOpenSource<AppScreen>) {","    analytics.trackScreenOpened(\"Articles\", source: source.analyticsKind)","    analytics.observeStateChanges(of: store, screen: \"Articles\")","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackScreenOpened(_:source:)"},{"text":" sends one ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screen_opened"},{"text":" event. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"observeStateChanges(of:screen:)"},{"text":" uses the same ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withObservationTracking"},{"text":" mechanism ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateContainerView"},{"text":" uses to mirror a store, and sends a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screen_state_changed"},{"text":" event for every subsequent ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState"},{"text":" transition — call it once, right where you create or first observe the store. When a transition lands on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".error"},{"text":", the event also carries the error’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"localizedDescription"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It also times how long the screen spends in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".loading"},{"type":"text","text":": the moment the state leaves "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".loading"},{"type":"text","text":" for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".empty"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".error"},{"type":"text","text":", it sends a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screen_load_duration"},{"type":"text","text":" event ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent\/screenLoadDuration(screen:outcome:milliseconds:)"},{"type":"text","text":") with that outcome and the elapsed time in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"duration_ms"},{"type":"text","text":" — useful for a “how long do loads actually take, and how often do they end in an error” dashboard without hand-rolling a stopwatch around every "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"load(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" call."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"screen_state_changed"},{"text":" event landing on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".error"},{"text":" tells you a screen failed to load; it doesn’t tell you whether the user gave up or hit Retry. Call ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackRetryTapped(_:)"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent\/screenRetryTapped(screen:)","type":"reference"},{"text":") from the same ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onRetry"},{"text":" closure you pass to the Error placeholder, so that’s a distinct, countable event instead of indistinguishable from the screen’s initial ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".loading"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["ScreenStateView(store.state, onRetry: {","    analytics.trackRetryTapped(\"Articles\")","    Task { await store.load { try await api.fetchArticles() } }","}) { articles in","    ArticleList(articles)","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/loadNextPage(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" doesn’t move "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state"},{"type":"text","text":" off "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":" on either a success or a failure, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"observeStateChanges(of:screen:)"},{"type":"text","text":" has nothing to report for it — call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackNextPageLoaded(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackNextPageFailed(_:errorDescription:)"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent\/screenNextPageLoaded(screen:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent\/screenNextPageFailed(screen:errorDescription:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":") from the same place you call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadNextPage(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", mirroring how "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"trackRetryTapped(_:)"},{"text":" is called from ","type":"text"},{"code":"onRetry","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"code":["func loadMore() async {","    await store.loadNextPage { try await api.fetchArticles(page: nextPage) }","    if let error = store.loadNextPageError {","        analytics.trackNextPageFailed(\"Articles\", errorDescription: error.localizedDescription)","    } else {","        analytics.trackNextPageLoaded(\"Articles\")","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Both ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenOpenSource","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" expose an ","type":"text"},{"code":"analyticsKind","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" helper — a short, stable, payload-free name for the current case (","type":"text"},{"code":"\"loading\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"error\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"push\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"deep_link\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", …) — so you can build custom ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenAnalyticsEvent","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"s yourself for anything the built-in factories don’t cover.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/TrackingAnalytics","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"title":"Tracking Screen Analytics"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/Scre